course: dictionary
lesson: 5119
title: Intruders and where they do not belong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An intruder is someone or something that comes into a place where it is not wanted or not allowed. Read the words around it to find the clues. «They are guarding their babies, and you are the intruder.» The words guarding their babies tell you that someone is keeping its young safe, so the intruder is the one who should not be there.
explain: Intruder is a noun, so you can have one intruder or many intruders. In a story, the word often makes you feel nervous, because you wonder what the intruder will do. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Stingless bees crowd and bite intruders» still makes sense if you think of intruders as things that come where they are not wanted.
explain: Some animals have their own ways of dealing with intruders. «Hoopoe chicks squirt smelly poo and a nasty oil at intruders, so predators remember never to try again.» The chicks drive away whatever comes too close to their nest. If you meet this word in a safety lesson, the clues will tell you what to do about it.
fact: An intruder is a person who goes into a place where they are not allowed, especially a building, to steal or cause harm.
fact: An intruder can also be an animal or thing that comes in where it is not wanted.
fact: «Intruders» means more than one intruder.
fact: Stingless bees bite and crowd intruders to defend their nest.
fact: If there is an intruder, tell an adult and call the emergency number: 999 in the UK and Ireland, 911 in the US and Canada, 000 in Australia, 111 in New Zealand.
exercise: «Stingless bees bite and crowd intruders to defend their nest.» What are intruders here? | Tiny stingers that hurt | Warm countries like Brazil | *Things that come where they are not wanted | Bees that make honey
exercise: «Hoopoe chicks squirt smelly poo and a nasty oil at intruders.» Why do the chicks do this? | To make a nice smell for their parents | To wash their nest | To show they are hungry | *To scare away whatever comes too close
exercise: «They are guarding their babies, and you are the intruder.» Which word tells you the parent is keeping its young safe? | intruder | *guarding | babies | they
test: What does an intruder do? | *Goes into a place where they are not allowed | Always stays at home | Waits outside for a friend to arrive | Makes a bed for the night
test: Which number should you call in the UK if there is an intruder? | 911 | *999 | 111 | 000
exam: Which phrase uses intruder correctly? | A sweet, sticky intruder on the picnic table | Friendly guest at a birthday party | An intruder who is always invited in | *An intruder alarm that sounds when someone breaks in
